      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local",
        "date": "2026-11-09T03:24:44Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(tools): spun holder-profile editor for milling tools\n\nA milling tool's holder can now be drawn as a revolved half-outline\n(points tip-up, straight or arc segments) in the tool editor's new\nProfile tab: Parametric (the holder cylinder of the numbers) or Custom\n(hand edits), a flat to-scale side view with flute/stickout/gauge\ndimensions, live refusals by name, and Apply profile - one undoable\nSetToolBody::spun. The drawn holder lands as a ToolBody whose envelope\nis the outline's exact bands (arcs flattened conservatively), so every\n#368 law, the stamp and the sim assembly read it. Saved as an optional\n`spun` key beside the facets (no project rung: a reader without it\njudges the facets, which can only over-report). Turning tools keep the\nBody section alone. Custom cutter/shank profiles are a follow-up.\n\nRefs #93\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
