      },
      "message": "Merge branch 'issue/371-tool-body-ui' (main at 5fd2b93a: #381, #395, #431, #422, #407, #420, #461) into issue/93-spun-tool-editor\n\nConflicts:\n- crates/tools/src/lib.rs: kept all modules - `spun` (#93) beside main's\n  `lathe_holder` (#369) and `lathe_insert_zone` (#396).\n- crates/app/src/schema.rs: ToolBody carries both main's `frame:\n  BodyFrame` (Spindle / Lathe, replacing axis/offset/profile) and this\n  branch's `spun: Option<SpunProfile>`; `ToolBody::profile()` stays the\n  spindle-envelope read.\n- crates/app/src/tool_body.rs: both imports; `build` lands\n  `BodyFrame::Spindle { .. }` with `spun: None`; `build_spun` now builds\n  a spindle-frame body (axis +Z, offset 0, the profile's exact bands).\n- crates/app/src/project/tool_body_wire.rs: ToolBodyDto keeps main's\n  optional `axis`/`offset`, `lathe` and `insert_zone` keys AND the\n  additive `spun` key. from_body writes `spun` on a spindle body and\n  never on a lathe one; to_body re-draws a `spun` body first and\n  refuses `spun` beside `lathe`/`insert_zone` by name, else main's\n  spindle/lathe dispatch. Module doc keeps all three notes.\n\nSemantic fix-ups: tool_body_lathe::build sets `spun: None`;\ntool_body_view::spun_preview's probe body takes a spindle frame;\ntests/tool_spun_profile reads `profile()` instead of the old field.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
