  {
    "sha": "729a1bc09dbe4413d7282e6c3d122fe2a673635a",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDcyOWExYmMwOWRiZTQ0MTNkNzI4MmU2YzNkMTIyZmUyYTY3MzYzNWE",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local",
        "date": "2026-11-09T19:34:49Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local",
        "date": "2026-11-09T19:39:18Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(tools): a zero-height spike stays in the spun profile's envelope\n\nSpunProfile::bands() dropped every non-climbing segment of the outline,\ntrusting the bands either side to hold both radii at that height. A\nflange drawn out and straight back at one z with no band above (the\ntop), below (the foot) or reaching it (mid-body) fell out of the\nenvelope: (55,0) (55,25) (90,25) (90,35) (90,0) showed holder Ø70 in\nthe Profile summary but was judged at r 25. A flat step's larger radius\nis now folded into the band touching its height (the one ending there\nfirst) when no touching band already reaches it - a plain step still\nreads exactly. The summary reads the new SpunProfile::max_radius, the\nsame number the widest band now carries.\n\nPinned by spun::tests::a_zero_height_spike_stays_in_the_envelope and\ntool_spun_profile::a_flat_top_flange_is_judged_at_its_full_radius (both\nfail before the fix).\n\nRefs #93\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
