      "message": "fix(tools): the tool editor's to-scale preview follows the drawn profile\n\nThe middle \"what verify would collide\" preview read the tool_body_ui\ndraft, re-mirrored from the world only inside the Body tab's section.\nWith the Profile tab showing it drew the plain cylinder after Apply\nprofile and after reload, and kept the drawn envelope after Cmd+Z. The\npreview's envelope() now re-syncs the draft first (a no-op unless the\nworld's body changed), so it follows Apply, undo and reload whichever\ntab shows.\n\nAlso: an Apply profile refusal stayed on screen after the outline was\ncorrected. The refused outline is remembered; once the draft moves off\nit and validates, that refusal retires (banner and status line). A\nrefusal of the very outline still on screen stands.\n\nPinned by egui_app::tests::tool_profile::\nthe_to_scale_preview_follows_the_profile_without_the_body_tab and\na_profile_refusal_retires_when_the_outline_validates (both fail before\nthe fix).\n\nRefs #93\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
